WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:06.281
I am Shahrazad, the wife of the king of Persia.

2
00:00:06.321 --> 00:00:08.322
I am not the king's first wife.

3
00:00:08.402 --> 00:00:08.742
Oh no!

4
00:00:08.802 --> 00:00:09.682
He has had hundreds of wives!

5
00:00:09.702 --> 00:00:10.182
I will explain.

6
00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:35.092
For years, each and every day the king would marry a beautiful young woman.

7
00:00:36.113 --> 00:00:40.276
Then the very next morning, he would order her to be killed!

8
00:00:42.198 --> 00:00:45.180
The people in the kingdom became very angry at this.

9
00:00:46.261 --> 00:00:50.705
Mothers and fathers cried, and all the young women shook with fear.

10
00:00:51.886 --> 00:00:53.767
No one wanted to marry the king.

11
00:00:54.768 --> 00:00:59.352
But unfortunately a king may do whatever he wants.

12
00:01:01.168 --> 00:01:04.891
One day it was my turn, and I became his bride.

13
00:01:06.573 --> 00:01:10.015
But as you can see, I am still alive.

14
00:01:11.477 --> 00:01:16.100
On the night of the day we were married, I kissed the king and said, "Shall I tell

15
00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.122
you a story to pass the time, sire?"

16
00:01:18.142 --> 00:01:20.664
"I love stories!"

17
00:01:21.164 --> 00:01:21.585
he said.

18
00:01:23.226 --> 00:01:26.669
So I told him a very good tale full of adventure.

19
00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.112
And the king listened all night.

20
00:01:31.308 --> 00:01:37.373
When I came to the end of the story, the king clapped his hands and said, "Oh, what

21
00:01:37.393 --> 00:01:38.434
a fine story!

22
00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:41.297
Please tell me another one, right now."

23
00:01:42.998 --> 00:01:47.262
Just then the sun peeked through the window, and a rooster crowed.

24
00:01:47.282 --> 00:01:50.705
"I am sorry, husband," I said.

25
00:01:50.725 --> 00:01:54.708
"The night is over, and there is no time left.

26
00:01:55.669 --> 00:02:01.806
But if you let me live, tonight I will tell an even better story."

27
00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.548
So the king did not kill me that day.

28
00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:10.912
That night, I told him a very long story.

29
00:02:12.313 --> 00:02:16.095
It was so long that when morning came, I was not finished.

30
00:02:17.456 --> 00:02:22.060
The king had to spare my life again so that he could hear how the story ended!

31
00:02:25.742 --> 00:02:28.244
So it has gone on, night after night.

32
00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:35.103
At sunrise, he lets me live another day so he can hear another exciting story.

33
00:02:36.484 --> 00:02:39.245
Would you like to hear one of the king's favorite stories?

34
00:02:40.546 --> 00:02:46.630
Yes? Then I will tell you all about Aladdin and his wonderful lamp.

35
00:02:49.131 --> 00:02:53.874
Long ago, a poor tailor lived in a faraway land by a great sea.

36
00:02:55.755 --> 00:03:00.878
This tailor had a son named Aladdin, who wanted to do nothing but play.

37
00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:09.344
When Aladdin was ten years old, the tailor said, "Son, you must learn a trade.

38
00:03:09.904 --> 00:03:12.026
I will teach you to be a tailor like me."

39
00:03:12.046 --> 00:03:16.749
"I don't want to work," Aladdin grumbled.

40
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:23.113
Every time the tailor turned his back, Aladdin would run out the door to play.

41
00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:25.275
"Come back!"

42
00:03:25.655 --> 00:03:28.866
the tailor called, but the boy would not obey.

43
00:03:30.807 --> 00:03:34.330
Aladdin's father was so sad that he became ill.

44
00:03:35.772 --> 00:03:37.994
He soon died of a broken heart.

45
00:03:40.636 --> 00:03:43.178
Aladdin and his mother were alone in the world.

46
00:03:43.198 --> 00:03:51.705
"All day I spin yarn so I can buy bread," sighed his mother, who was named Zeba.

47
00:03:51.725 --> 00:03:54.548
"You play all day.

48
00:03:55.852 --> 00:03:58.034
You come home only when you are hungry!"

49
00:04:00.056 --> 00:04:04.260
And that is how things remained until Aladdin was seventeen years old.

50
00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:09.445
That year a stranger named Magrib came to the city.

51
00:04:10.706 --> 00:04:13.148
Nobody knew that Magrib was a magician.

52
00:04:14.309 --> 00:04:15.710
That was his secret.

53
00:04:17.892 --> 00:04:21.676
One day Magrib was watching the children who played in the streets.

54
00:04:23.104 --> 00:04:26.926
His pale eyes shone beneath the hood of his dusty robe.

55
00:04:28.047 --> 00:04:29.388
He pointed to Aladdin.

56
00:04:29.408 --> 00:04:32.009
"Who is that boy?"

57
00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:35.191
he whispered to a nearby child.

58
00:04:35.211 --> 00:04:37.472
"Who is his father?"

59
00:04:39.913 --> 00:04:42.195
"That's Aladdin," the child said.

60
00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.616
"He's the tailor's son."

61
00:04:45.897 --> 00:04:49.379
Magrib asked many questions.

62
00:04:49.399 --> 00:04:51.540
He learned everything about Aladdin.

63
00:04:52.756 --> 00:04:54.238
Then he smiled.

64
00:04:54.258 --> 00:04:57.222
"My search is over!"

65
00:04:57.803 --> 00:04:58.724
said the magician.

66
00:04:58.744 --> 00:05:01.647
"I have found him!"
